## Binding playbook
Read `video-playbook/README.md` first, then the file for the task at hand. Its rules are defaults backed by real failures; deviate only with a stated reason.

## Rules
- Work silent and headless: Playwright with `--mute-audio`, no GUI windows, no audio playback. Verify with frame sheets, loudness meters and transcripts.
- Measure, never estimate: word onsets (whisper + silence snap), loudness, crops, fps and frame counts.
- `brand/brand.json` is the only source for colors, fonts, type scale, motion and safe zones. Use the real logo, icon and fonts; never redraw brand assets.
- Every asset needs a licence entry (`library/*/index.json`); the build fails without one. No ripped footage, no commercial songs in exports.
- Fail loud: a missing asset, unmocked API, console error or silent bed stops the build. No placeholders ship.
- Demo and capture data comes from seeded demo accounts on staging, never real users.
- Every on-screen claim (price, limits, "free") must match the product's real config: <link or file>.
- Git holds code, specs, scripts and research. Media (renders, audio, footage) is gitignored.
- After every render: run `qa/`, then report the QA.md summary, a contact sheet and the board path.
- When I correct something, update brand.json, the engine defaults or `video-playbook/` so it doesn't recur.
- One heavy render, TTS or whisper job at a time.

## Commands
- Build: `<node engine/render.mjs videos/<slug>/spec.json --shapes 9x16,16x9,1x1>`
- QA: `<node qa/qa.mjs videos/<slug>/out>`
- Board: `<python board/build.py>` → open `board/index.html`

